DESCRIPTION >
    Nightly-attribution conversion row-pull. Port of the nightly's per-site
    conversionsQuery (api/jobs/nightly-attribution.js processSite, :396-413) — the
    original 14-column shape the nightly maps positionally (uuid, distinct_id, timestamp
    + the 11 properties at :396-405), PLUS one KI-62 column appended last (15th):
    original_conversion_event_id. One row per $conversion, site-scoped, windowed,
    ORDER BY timestamp ASC LIMIT 1000 (matching the nightly exactly, NOT the DESC/10000
    of the live-read siblings).

    KI-62 (write-path PR): original_conversion_event_id is the bag pointer a refund
    stamps to the ORIGINAL conversion it reverses (stripe-refund.js / shopify-refund.js).
    It is APPENDED LAST and the nightly maps by NAME (mapConversionPipeRow), so this is
    purely additive: the current 14-field consumer ignores it. The nightly consumer that
    READS it (verbatim-inheritance) is the SEPARATE KI-62 inheritance PR; this pipe change
    only makes the pointer reach the nightly and does NOT deploy here (founder-gated).

    §2.6 typed-column translation (events.datasource): properties.site_id -> site_id,
    event -> event_type, uuid -> event_id (no `uuid` column; event_id is the Tinybird
    identifier). TYPED columns: distinct_id, timestamp, conversion_type, conversion_value,
    external_event_id, webhook_customer_id, stripe_subscription_id, stripe_invoice_id,
    currency, occurred_at, provider. BAG-only (no typed column, JSONExtractString):
    provider_event_id, stripe_event_type, original_conversion_event_id. The ''-vs-NULL
    bag trap is INERT for all —
    the nightly consumer collapses via `row[10] || null` / `row[12] || null`, so plain
    JSONExtractString (no nullIf) is faithful; there is no count(DISTINCT ...) here.
    MONEY: conversion_value = toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) (ClickHouse
    dialect) == the live parseFloat(properties.conversion_value) the nightly applies.

    DateTime params interpolate directly ({{DateTime(p, required=True)}}, no toDateTime
    wrapper). site_id is required=True — a conversions row-pull must NEVER fall through
    to a default/all-tenant scope (§6.5).

    VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN — founder/orchestrator value-gates vs live HogQL before wiring.

NODE nightly_conversions_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        event_id AS uuid,
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        conversion_type,
        toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) AS conversion_value,
        external_event_id,
        webhook_customer_id,
        stripe_subscription_id,
        stripe_invoice_id,
        currency,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'provider_event_id') AS provider_event_id,
        occurred_at,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'stripe_event_type') AS stripe_event_type,
        provider,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'original_conversion_event_id') AS original_conversion_event_id
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY timestamp ASC
    LIMIT 1000

TYPE endpoint
